    <DataNode elementId="AT5G26667-MONOMER" textLabel="UMP/CMP kinase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O04905" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="515" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The cDNA encoding a UMP/CMP kinase catalyzing the phosphorylation of uridine-5&apos;-monophosphate (UMP) to form uridine-5&apos;-diphosphate (UDP) was isolated from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. The enzyme expressed a comparable activity towards cytidine-5&apos;-monophosphate (CMP) to form the corresponding diphosphate (CDP) and was therefore named UMP/CMP kinase. The data obtained fit a random Bi-Bi reaction mechanism. The molecular function was confirmed twofold, first by functional complementation of a UMP/CMP kinase deficient yeast mutant and second by characterization of the recombinant protein expressed in and purified from &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [9576794]|. Site-directed mutagenesis demonstrated the importance of the characteristic glycine-rich sequence GGPG(S/A)GK for ATP binding and enzyme catalysis |CITS: [9784243]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G26667-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G26667.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Panther" value="PTHR23359" />
